IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-title`

-- Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters, over the baseline's rules in tla-title.l4.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES (type `Seat`; the baseline already declares a type `Role`, the capacity in which someone claims a deceased's
-- land, and a second `Role` cannot be declared beside it, so the seat's type is named `Seat`; the parameter is still
-- `my role`):
--   * `I own registered land, or a share in it` -- the baseline's seat: the registered proprietor, a joint tenant or
--     tenant in common, the mortgagor;
--   * `I am buying registered land` -- the baseline's seat: the buyer about to become the proprietor;
--   * `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` -- the baseline's seat
--     as it meets a death (c087, c096, d093): the surviving joint proprietor, the executor or administrator, the devisee;
--   * `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` -- new: the mortgagee, which the Act gives the notice, sale and
--     foreclosure powers (ss 105AA, 106-109, 113, 121-123);
--   * `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` -- new: the caveator (ss 137-142).
-- The Registrar, the Commissioner and the Supreme Court are never a seat; what they may or must do appears as what it
-- means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (graffiti design D8). Within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that situation's
-- fact straight after `my role` (a second situation straight after the first), and answers `does not arise for you`
-- when it does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, the same name,
-- type and @desc. They are, by the provision the Act ties the rule to:
--   * owner: `there is a mortgage over my land` (ss 58, 88-131 -- the twelve mortgage questions), and within it
--     `I am in default under my mortgage` (ss 106-108, 109, 121, 122 -- the six that follow a default);
--     `a caveat has been lodged against my land` (ss 138-142 -- five); `I own the land with someone else` (ss 60, 61 --
--     three); `I have lost my land, or an interest in it, through fraud, error, misdescription or someone else's
--     registration` (ss 201, 211 -- two);
--   * owner and buyer: `someone holds or claims a lease of the land` (s 68(1A) -- the two lease questions);
--   * buyer: `I take the land subject to a mortgage that stays on the title` (s 88); `I am buying at a sale by a lender
--     under its power of sale` (s 110);
--   * survivor, executor or beneficiary: `my capacity` (the baseline's `Role`: s 227 for the survivor, s 187 for the
--     executor or administrator, s 220 for the devisee); the route question takes it as an ordinary input;
--   * lender: `the owner is in default under my mortgage` (ss 106-109, 121, 122 -- six);
--   * caveator: `I have been served with notice that the owner has applied to register a dealing` (s 138(3));
--     `the Registrar has served me with a notice that my caveat will lapse in 21 days` (s 138B); `my earlier caveat over
--     this land has come to an end` (s 138D).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- Every helper here that reads a situation enumeration lists every value with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31), so
-- an ASSUMEd value read in the cases fails instead of passing silently.
--
-- The rules are the baseline's; this module calls them and restates none. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT
-- input. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Seat IS ONE OF
    `I own registered land, or a share in it`
    `I am buying registered land`
    `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died`
    `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land`
    `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `months` HAS `the number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Whether I am bound` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `bound: section 68 does not free you from it`
    `free: section 68 frees you from it`
    `unprotected: your title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees you from nothing`
    `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation`

DECLARE `My route onto the register` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `you may apply as survivor under section 227; no probate is needed`
    `you may apply as executor or administrator under section 187, on the probate or letters`
    `you may apply as devisee under section 219, producing the will or probate`
    `section 227 is the survivor's route; whether the deceased's estate keeps any interest is general law, not this Act`
    `this Act gives you no route onto the register for this land in that capacity`
    `the land is not under this Act, which says nothing about it`

DECLARE `What my mortgage does` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `it is a security over your land; you remain the proprietor and the land is not transferred`

§§ `Building the answers from the baseline's`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `the answer` IS A Bound
GIVETH A `Whether I am bound`
`the s 68 answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `bound: section 68 does not free me from it` THEN `bound: section 68 does not free you from it`
    WHEN `free: section 68 frees me from it` THEN `free: section 68 frees you from it`
    WHEN `unprotected: my title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees me from nothing` THEN `unprotected: your title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees you from nothing`
    WHEN `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation` THEN `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation`

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A `My route onto the register`
`the route answer` `the route` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `I may apply as survivor under section 227; no probate is needed` THEN `you may apply as survivor under section 227; no probate is needed`
    WHEN `I may apply as executor or administrator under section 187, on the probate or letters` THEN `you may apply as executor or administrator under section 187, on the probate or letters`
    WHEN `I may apply as devisee under section 219, producing the will or probate` THEN `you may apply as devisee under section 219, producing the will or probate`
    WHEN `section 227 is the survivor's route; whether the deceased's estate keeps any interest is general law, not this Act` THEN `section 227 is the survivor's route; whether the deceased's estate keeps any interest is general law, not this Act`
    WHEN `this Act gives me no route onto the register for this land in that capacity` THEN `this Act gives you no route onto the register for this land in that capacity`
    WHEN `the land is not under this Act, which says nothing about it` THEN `the land is not under this Act, which says nothing about it`

-- The baseline's mortgage record, from four plain answers.
GIVEN `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lender signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owner signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `owner signed before registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Mortgage
`the mortgage from` `is registered` `lender signed` `owner signed` `owner signed before registration` MEANS
    Mortgage WITH
        `registered` IS `is registered`
        `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` IS `lender signed`
        `a lodged counterpart is signed by me` IS `owner signed`
        `I signed a counterpart before registration` IS `owner signed before registration`

§§ `The situations a question arises in`

-- The death situation: the capacity in which I claim (the baseline's `Role`). Each helper lists every value, with no
-- OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `my capacity` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I claim as the survivor` IF
    CONSIDER `my capacity`
    WHEN `the surviving joint proprietor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the executor or administrator` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a devisee under the will` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `my capacity` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I claim as executor or administrator` IF
    CONSIDER `my capacity`
    WHEN `the surviving joint proprietor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the executor or administrator` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a devisee under the will` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `my capacity` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I claim as devisee` IF
    CONSIDER `my capacity`
    WHEN `the surviving joint proprietor` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the executor or administrator` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a devisee under the will` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN FALSE

§§ `For the owner of registered land, or of a share in it`

§§§ `ss 53, 68, 134 -- what my registered title is free of, and who comes first`

@export Does my instrument have priority over another instrument affecting the same land, whatever their dates and whatever anyone knew (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 53(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the time my instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc When your instrument (your transfer, mortgage or other dealing) was registered, on any consistent clock, for example minutes since some moment
      `the time the other instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc When the other instrument was registered, on the same clock
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my registered instrument come first` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN `yes if` (`Does my instrument have priority` `the time my instrument was registered` `the time the other instrument was registered`)
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN `yes if` (`Does my instrument have priority` `the time my instrument was registered` `the time the other instrument was registered`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I bound by this interest in my land though it is not on my title, or is my registered title free of it (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 68, 134)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the interest` IS AN Interest @desc The interest someone claims against the land
      `my title is a case of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find your title a case of fraud (s 68 does not define fraud; knowing of an unregistered interest is not of itself fraud, s 134)
GIVETH A `Whether I am bound`
`Does this interest bind my registered title` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN `the s 68 answer` (`Am I bound by this interest` `the interest` `my title is a case of fraud`)
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN `the s 68 answer` (`Am I bound by this interest` `the interest` `my title is a case of fraud`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I hold the land subject to this lease, though it may not be registered (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 68(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone holds or claims a lease of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone holds, or claims, a lease or agreement for lease of the land
      `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease is registered on the title
      `the lease came before my interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease (or agreement for lease) existed before your interest
      `term of the lease in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of the lease, in years
      `the tenant is in actual possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tenant is actually in possession of the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I hold my land subject to this lease` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `someone holds or claims a lease of the land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do I take subject to the lease` `the lease is registered` `the lease came before my interest` `term of the lease in years` `the tenant is in actual possession`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN
        IF `someone holds or claims a lease of the land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do I take subject to the lease` `the lease is registered` `the lease came before my interest` `term of the lease in years` `the tenant is in actual possession`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the tenant's option to buy or to renew valid against me as the later registered owner (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 68(1A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone holds or claims a lease of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone holds, or claims, a lease or agreement for lease of the land
      `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease is registered on the title
      `the lease is protected by caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat protecting the lease is lodged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the tenant's option valid against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `someone holds or claims a lease of the land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the option valid against me` `the lease is registered` `the lease is protected by caveat`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN
        IF `someone holds or claims a lease of the land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is the option valid against me` `the lease is registered` `the lease is protected by caveat`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 199, 201, 202, 211, 214A -- who can take the land from me, and who pays when it is lost`

-- Every owner can be met by a claim, so this question takes no situation input.
@export Can this person bring an action to recover my land from me, or is my certificate of title a bar (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 199, 202)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A Claim @desc Who is claiming the land, and on what footing
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can this claimant take my land from me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN `yes if` (`Can this person recover my land from me` `the claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 201: the situation is the deprivation itself, so the baseline's first input is TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export I have lost my land: can I recover damages from the State, through an action against the Registrar as nominal defendant (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 201; s 196, cases where the State is not liable, is not covered)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have lost my land, or an interest in it, through fraud, error, misdescription or someone else's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lost land, or an interest in land, through fraud, the bringing of land under the Act, the registration of someone else as proprietor, or an error or misdescription in the register
      `the person liable is dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who acquired title through it is dead
      `the person liable is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person has been adjudged bankrupt
      `the person liable cannot be found in the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person cannot be found within the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court
      `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person sold on bona fide for value, so that s 201(2) caps what they must pay
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I recover damages from the State for my lost land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `I have lost my land, or an interest in it, through fraud, error, misdescription or someone else's registration`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I recover damages from the State` TRUE `the person liable is dead` `the person liable is bankrupt` `the person liable cannot be found in the jurisdiction` `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have lost my land: is it still time to sue the State for damages (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 211: 6 years; for a minor or a person of unsound mind, 6 years after the disability ends, within 30 years)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have lost my land, or an interest in it, through fraud, error, misdescription or someone else's registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lost land, or an interest in land, through fraud, the bringing of land under the Act, the registration of someone else as proprietor, or an error or misdescription in the register
      `months since I was deprived` IS A NUMBER @desc Months from the date you lost the land to now
      `I was under a disability when deprived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a minor or of unsound mind when you lost the land
      `months since the disability ceased` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, months since the disability ended (0 if it has not ended or does not apply)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is there still time to sue for my lost land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `I have lost my land, or an interest in it, through fraud, error, misdescription or someone else's registration`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is it still time to sue for my land` `months since I was deprived` `I was under a disability when deprived` `months since the disability ceased`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is a certificate of title or instrument procured by fraud void against me (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 214A: void against every party to the fraud, whether or not anyone is convicted)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `it was procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate, instrument or entry was procured or made by fraud in a circumstance set out in s 214
      `I was party to the fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to that fraud
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the fraudulent title void against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN `yes if` (`Is it void against me` `it was procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` `I was party to the fraud`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 60, 61 -- owning with someone else`

@export Are my co-owner and I joint tenants (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 60; that the survivor takes the whole is general law, not the Act's text)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I own the land with someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered as proprietor of the land together with one or more other people
      `how we are registered` IS A Holding @desc How you and your co-owner(s) are registered on the title
      `number registered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many proprietors are registered
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are my co-owner and I joint tenants` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `I own the land with someone else`
        THEN `yes if` (`Are we joint tenants` `how we are registered` `number registered`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my co-owners and I take a separate certificate of title for each of our undivided shares (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 60)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I own the land with someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered as proprietor of the land together with one or more other people
      `how we are registered` IS A Holding @desc How you and your co-owner(s) are registered on the title
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we each take a certificate for our share` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `I own the land with someone else`
        THEN `yes if` (`May we take separate certificates for our shares` `how we are registered`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 61(3) bars only "persons other than the proprietors registered". The person in this role is a registered
-- proprietor, so the baseline's `I am a registered proprietor` is TRUE by the role's own terms, and the answer is yes
-- once "no survivorship" is known: the words do not stop the registered owners dealing.
@export "No survivorship" is on our title: may I deal with the property without a court's or the Commissioner's order (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 61(3), which bars only people other than the registered proprietors)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I own the land with someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered as proprietor of the land together with one or more other people
      `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the words "no survivorship" have been entered on the title and signed by the Registrar
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I deal with our land despite no survivorship` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `I own the land with someone else`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I deal with the property` `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar` TRUE FALSE)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 58, 105, 105AA, 106(1), 113, 123, 131 -- my mortgage`

@export Does the mortgage over my land bind me, though I never signed what was lodged (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 58, 105(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage is registered
      `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a counterpart lodged for registration was signed by the lender (the person who becomes the proprietor of the mortgage)
      `a lodged counterpart is signed by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a counterpart signed by you was also lodged
      `I signed a counterpart before registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed a counterpart of the mortgage before it was registered
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I bound by the mortgage over my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my mortgage bind me` (`the mortgage from` `the mortgage is registered` `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` `a lodged counterpart is signed by me` `I signed a counterpart before registration`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my lender lodge my mortgage electronically (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 105AA: only if the lender has signed it and holds a counterpart I signed)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `the lender has signed the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender has signed the mortgage instrument
      `the lender holds a counterpart I signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender holds a counterpart of the mortgage signed by you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my mortgage be lodged electronically` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my lender lodge my mortgage electronically` `the lender has signed the mortgage` `the lender holds a counterpart I signed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What does registering my mortgage do to my title (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
GIVETH A `What my mortgage does`
`What does my mortgage do to my title` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN CONSIDER `What does my registered mortgage do`
             WHEN `a security over my land; I remain the proprietor and the land is not transferred` THEN `it is a security over your land; you remain the proprietor and the land is not transferred`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my mortgage bind me to this, though it does not say so: to pay, to repair, to let the lender inspect, to insure (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 113, 115, 131)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `the covenant` IS A Covenant @desc What you are asked whether you must do
      `the mortgage negatives or modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage expressly negatives or modifies that implied covenant (s 131)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I do this under my mortgage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does my mortgage bind me to this` `the covenant` `the mortgage negatives or modifies it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have paid off my mortgage: is my land freed from it yet (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 123: only when the Registrar enters a discharge the lender signed before a witness)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `the lender signed a witnessed discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender signed a discharge of the mortgage, attested by a witness
      `the Registrar has entered the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has entered the discharge in the Register
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my land free of the mortgage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Is my land freed from the mortgage` `the lender signed a witnessed discharge` `the Registrar has entered the discharge`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many months must a default under my mortgage continue before my lender may serve me a notice to pay (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(1): one month, or the period the mortgage fixes)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage expressly fixes before a notice to pay, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Months`
`How long must my default last before a notice to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN `months` (`How many months before a notice to pay` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 106-110, 121, 122 -- my default, the notice, sale and foreclosure`

@export I am in default: may my lender serve me a notice to pay (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage is registered
      `months my default has continued` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your default has continued
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage expressly fixes before a notice to pay, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be served a notice to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN `yes if` (`May my lender serve a notice to pay` `the mortgage is registered` `months my default has continued` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am in default: has the notice to pay been properly served on me (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(2): personally, by registered post, left on the land, or a prescribed electronic way; ordinary post is not service)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `how the notice was sent` IS A Service @desc How the lender sent or gave the notice to pay
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was the notice to pay properly served on me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN `yes if` (`Was the notice properly served on me` `how the notice was sent`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am in default: may my lender sell my land (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 106-108: one month after a notice properly served, or a written demand where the money is payable on demand, or the period the mortgage fixes)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the money is payable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage makes the money payable on demand
      `a written demand was made under the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender made a written demand under the mortgage
      `a notice to pay was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender served a notice to pay
      `how the notice was sent` IS A Service @desc How the lender sent or gave the notice to pay
      `months the default continued after the notice or demand` IS A NUMBER @desc Months the default has continued since the notice or demand
      `months fixed by the mortgage for sale` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage fixes after notice before sale, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my land be sold by my lender` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN `yes if` (`May my lender sell my land` `the money is payable on demand` `a written demand was made under the mortgage` `a notice to pay was served` `how the notice was sent` `months the default continued after the notice or demand` `months fixed by the mortgage for sale`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My lender sold my land: how much of the sale money comes to me (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 109(1): the surplus after the sale expenses, the selling mortgage and later mortgages and charges)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the sale price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price the land sold for, in dollars
      `the expenses of the sale and default` IS A NUMBER @desc The expenses of and incidental to the sale and consequent on the default, in dollars
      `what is owing on the mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is due or owing on the mortgage under which the land was sold, in dollars
      `what is owing on later mortgages and charges` IS A NUMBER @desc What is owing on mortgages and charges registered after it, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the sale money is mine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN amount (`How much of the sale money comes to me` `the sale price` `the expenses of the sale and default` `what is owing on the mortgage` `what is owing on later mortgages and charges`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am in default: may my lender apply to foreclose my right to redeem (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 121: 6 months' default and a failed auction first)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `months the default has continued after the time for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the time for payment in the mortgage, with the default continuing
      `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensed auctioneer offered the land at public auction after a notice to pay was served under s 106
      `the auction raised too little or drew no bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the highest bid was not enough to pay the mortgage money and expenses, or there was no bid
      `notice of intention to foreclose was served on the mortgagor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgagor (the owner) was served with notice of the lender's intention to apply for foreclosure
      `notice was served on every later registered interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone with a later interest on the Register was served with the same notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my lender seek foreclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN `yes if` (`May my lender apply to foreclose` `months the default has continued after the time for payment` `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay` `the auction raised too little or drew no bid` `notice of intention to foreclose was served on the mortgagor` `notice was served on every later registered interest`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am in default: can a foreclosure order now issue and take my land free of my right to redeem (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 122)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `there is a mortgage over my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your land, or your share of it, is mortgaged (a mortgage registered, or being registered, to secure money you owe)
      `I am in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed to pay money due under the mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the Commissioner directed the advertisements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed the advertisements offering the land for private sale
      `months since the first advertisement` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the first advertisement
      `the time the Commissioner appointed has come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time the Commissioner appointed (at least one month after the first advertisement) has arrived
      `a sale in the interval raised enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sale in the meantime raised enough to pay the principal, interest and all expenses
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my land be foreclosed now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `there is a mortgage over my land`
        THEN IF `I am in default under my mortgage`
             THEN `yes if` (`Can a foreclosure order issue against me` `the Commissioner directed the advertisements` `months since the first advertisement` `the time the Commissioner appointed has come` `a sale in the interval raised enough`)
             ELSE `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 138-142 -- a caveat against my land`

@export Does this caveat stop my dealing being registered (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 139, 142)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a caveat has been lodged against my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has lodged a caveat against your land (now, or one that has since ended)
      `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat forbidding the dealing is in force on the title
      `it was lodged after my instrument was presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveat was lodged after the instrument was presented for registration
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises my dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a beneficiary's caveat: whether the Commissioner is of opinion the will or settlement authorises the dealing
      `the caveator consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator consents to the registration
      `days since the caveator was served with notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the caveator was served with notice of the dealing
      `the caveator protested in writing in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator lodged a written protest within 14 days of being served
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the caveat block my dealing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `a caveat has been lodged against my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Does the caveat stop my dealing` `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing` `it was lodged after my instrument was presented` `the kind of caveat` `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises my dealing` `the caveator consents` `days since the caveator was served with notice` `the caveator protested in writing in time`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have applied to register a dealing: has the caveat lapsed, 14 days after the caveator was served with notice of my application (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 138(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a caveat has been lodged against my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has lodged a caveat against your land (now, or one that has since ended)
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `I applied to register a transfer or dealing and have not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to register a transfer or other dealing and the application stands
      `days since the caveator was served with notice of the application` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the caveator was served with notice of the application to register the dealing
      `a judge has ordered a further delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge, on the caveator's undertaking or security, directed the Registrar to delay registration
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the caveat lapsed on my application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `a caveat has been lodged against my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Has the caveat lapsed on my dealing` `the kind of caveat` `I applied to register a transfer or dealing and have not withdrawn` `days since the caveator was served with notice of the application` `a judge has ordered a further delay`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Has the caveat lapsed after the 21-day notice I had the Registrar serve on the caveator (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 138A, 138B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a caveat has been lodged against my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has lodged a caveat against your land (now, or one that has since ended)
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the Registrar served the caveator with my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on your application, the Registrar served the caveator with the s 138B notice
      `days since the 21-day notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the s 138B notice was served on the caveator
      `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator obtained a Supreme Court order extending the caveat and lodged a copy with the Registrar
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has the caveat lapsed on my 21-day notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `a caveat has been lodged against my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Has the caveat lapsed on my notice` `the kind of caveat` `the Registrar served the caveator with my notice` `days since the 21-day notice was served` `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The caveat has ended: may the caveator lodge another caveat against my land (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 138D)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a caveat has been lodged against my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has lodged a caveat against your land (now, or one that has since ended)
      `how the caveat ended` IS A CaveatEnd @desc How the earlier caveat came to an end
      `the owner's consent is endorsed on the new caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered proprietor's consent is endorsed on the further caveat
      `the Supreme Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court gave leave for the further caveat and the order was served on the Registrar
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the caveator caveat my land again` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `a caveat has been lodged against my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the caveator lodge another caveat` `how the caveat ended` `the owner's consent is endorsed on the new caveat` `the Supreme Court gave leave`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be compensated for a caveat lodged against my land without reasonable cause (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 140; the amount is for a judge)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a caveat has been lodged against my land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone has lodged a caveat against your land (now, or one that has since ended)
      `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause
      `the owner suffered damage from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person complaining (here, the owner) suffered damage because of the caveat, for example a lost or delayed sale
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be compensated for a caveat on my land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own registered land, or a share in it` THEN
        IF `a caveat has been lodged against my land`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can I be compensated for the caveat` `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` `the owner suffered damage from it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the buyer of registered land`

§§§ `ss 52(2), 58, 146-149 -- when the land passes to me`

@export I have settled: has the land passed to me under my transfer (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 52(2), 58: registration, not settlement, passes it)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `a memorandum of my transfer is entered in the Register on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has entered the memorandum of your transfer on the certificate of title (that is, it is registered)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the land mine yet` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN `yes if` (`Has the land passed to me` `a memorandum of my transfer is entered in the Register on the certificate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export With a 48-hour stay, does my transfer take priority over anything lodged after my search, caveats included (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 148, 149)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am dealing for value with the proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying (or otherwise dealing for value) from the registered proprietor
      `the proprietor consented in writing to the stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proprietor (or their agent authorised in writing) consented in writing to your stay application
      `the search showed the proprietor free to deal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the search certificate showed the proprietor free to deal with the land
      `hours from the search certificate time to my lodging` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours between the time stated in the search certificate and the lodging of your transfer
      `my transfer was properly perfected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your transfer was complete and in order for registration when lodged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my stay give my transfer priority` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN `yes if` (`Does my transfer take priority under the stay` `I am dealing for value with the proprietor` `the proprietor consented in writing to the stay` `the search showed the proprietor free to deal` `hours from the search certificate time to my lodging` `my transfer was properly perfected`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 88, 110, 131 -- buying land under a mortgage, or from a lender`

-- s 88: the situation is the mortgage staying on the title, so the baseline's first input is TRUE by its own terms.
@export I am taking the land subject to the seller's mortgage: must I indemnify the seller against it (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 88, 131)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I take the land subject to a mortgage that stays on the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your transfer is subject to a registered mortgage that stays on the title after it
      `the transfer negatives or modifies the covenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer expressly negatives or modifies the covenant s 88 implies
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I indemnify the seller against the mortgage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN
        IF `I take the land subject to a mortgage that stays on the title`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I indemnify the seller` TRUE `the transfer negatives or modifies the covenant`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I am buying at a lender's sale: do I take free of this encumbrance (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 110)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am buying at a sale by a lender under its power of sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the seller is a mortgagee selling under its power of sale
      `it is the mortgage under which the land was sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the encumbrance is the selling lender's own mortgage
      `it was registered after that mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was registered after the selling lender's mortgage
      `it is a lease or easement the lender consented to in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a lease, easement, carbon right, carbon covenant or plantation interest that the selling lender consented to in writing
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I buy free of this encumbrance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying registered land` THEN
        IF `I am buying at a sale by a lender under its power of sale`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do I take free of it` `it is the mortgage under which the land was sold` `it was registered after that mortgage` `it is a lease or easement the lender consented to in writing`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the survivor, executor or beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died`

§§§ `ss 187, 219, 220, 227 -- onto the register after a death`

-- The route arises in every capacity, so it takes `my capacity` as an ordinary input, after the facts the baseline
-- reads first; the other four take it straight after the role, as their situation.
@export How do I get onto the register for the land of someone who has died (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 187, 219, 227)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the land is under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is Western Australian land registered under the Transfer of Land Act (land overseas or elsewhere in Australia is not)
      `how the deceased held it` IS A Holding @desc How the deceased was registered: as a joint proprietor, a tenant in common, or sole proprietor
      `my capacity` IS A Role @desc In what capacity you claim the deceased's land: as the surviving joint proprietor, as the executor or administrator, as a devisee under the will, or none of these
GIVETH A `My route onto the register`
`What is my route onto the register after the death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` THEN `the route answer` (`How do I get onto the register after the death` `the land is under this Act` `how the deceased held it` `my capacity`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As the surviving joint proprietor, may the Commissioner direct my registration as proprietor, without probate (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 227)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `my capacity` IS A Role @desc In what capacity you claim the deceased's land: as the surviving joint proprietor, as the executor or administrator, as a devisee under the will, or none of these
      `the deceased was registered with me as joint proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deceased and you were registered as joint proprietors under this Act
      `I am the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are "the person entitled" (s 227 does not define it)
      `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have proved the death to the Commissioner's satisfaction
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be registered as the survivor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` THEN
        IF `I claim as the survivor` `my capacity`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be registered as survivor` `the deceased was registered with me as joint proprietor` `I am the person entitled` `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As executor or administrator, must the Registrar register me as proprietor of the deceased's interest (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 187(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `my capacity` IS A Role @desc In what capacity you claim the deceased's land: as the surviving joint proprietor, as the executor or administrator, as a devisee under the will, or none of these
      `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has received an office copy of the probate, letters of administration, or Public Trustee's order or election
      `I applied in writing to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied in writing to be registered as proprietor
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be registered as executor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` THEN
        IF `I claim as executor or administrator` `my capacity`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the Registrar register me as executor` `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` `I applied in writing to be registered`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As one of several executors or administrators, may we deal with the deceased's land (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 187(3): all of us must join)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `my capacity` IS A Role @desc In what capacity you claim the deceased's land: as the surviving joint proprietor, as the executor or administrator, as a devisee under the will, or none of these
      `number granted probate or administration` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were granted probate or administration
      `number joining in the dealing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them join in the dealing
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May we executors deal with the land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` THEN
        IF `I claim as executor or administrator` `my capacity`
        THEN `yes if` (`May we deal with the deceased's land` `number granted probate or administration` `number joining in the dealing`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a devisee who has applied under s 219, may the Registrar now register me (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 220: not less than 14 days after the advertisement, and no caveat forbidding it)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `my capacity` IS A Role @desc In what capacity you claim the deceased's land: as the surviving joint proprietor, as the executor or administrator, as a devisee under the will, or none of these
      `the Commissioner directed notice of my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed notice of your application to be published (rather than rejecting it)
      `days the Commissioner appointed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the advertisement that the Commissioner appointed
      `days since the first advertisement` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the (first) advertisement
      `a caveat forbids my registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat forbidding your registration has been lodged
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I be registered as the devisee` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the survivor, executor or a beneficiary of someone registered for land who has died` THEN
        IF `I claim as devisee` `my capacity`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I be registered as devisee` `the Commissioner directed notice of my application` `days the Commissioner appointed` `days since the first advertisement` `a caveat forbids my registration`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the lender on a mortgage`

§§§ `ss 58, 105, 105AA, 113, 123, 131 -- my mortgage`

@export Does my mortgage bind the owner of the land, though the owner signed none of what was lodged (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 58, 105(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage is registered
      `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a counterpart lodged for registration was signed by the lender (the person who becomes the proprietor of the mortgage)
      `a lodged counterpart is signed by the owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a counterpart signed by the owner of the land was also lodged
      `the owner signed a counterpart before registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner of the land signed a counterpart of the mortgage before it was registered
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my mortgage bind the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN `yes if` (`Does my mortgage bind me` (`the mortgage from` `the mortgage is registered` `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` `a lodged counterpart is signed by the owner` `the owner signed a counterpart before registration`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I lodge the mortgage electronically (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 105AA: only if I have signed it and hold a counterpart the owner signed)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have signed the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the lender, have signed the mortgage instrument
      `I hold a counterpart the owner signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a counterpart of the mortgage signed by the owner of the land
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I lodge the mortgage electronically` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN `yes if` (`May my lender lodge my mortgage electronically` `I have signed the mortgage` `I hold a counterpart the owner signed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the owner bound to this by my mortgage, though it does not say so: to pay, to repair, to let me inspect, to insure (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 113, 115, 131)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `what the owner may be bound to` IS A Covenant @desc What you are asked whether the owner must do
      `the mortgage negatives or modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage expressly negatives or modifies that implied covenant (s 131)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the owner do this under my mortgage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN `yes if` (`Does my mortgage bind me to this` `what the owner may be bound to` `the mortgage negatives or modifies it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The loan is repaid: when is the land freed from my mortgage (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 123: when the Registrar enters a discharge I signed before a witness)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I signed a witnessed discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed a discharge of the mortgage, attested by a witness
      `the Registrar has entered the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has entered the discharge in the Register
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the land freed from my mortgage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN `yes if` (`Is my land freed from the mortgage` `I signed a witnessed discharge` `the Registrar has entered the discharge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many months must the owner's default continue before I may serve a notice to pay (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(1): one month, or the period the mortgage fixes)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage expressly fixes before a notice to pay, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Months`
`How long must the default last before I serve a notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN `months` (`How many months before a notice to pay` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 106-109, 121, 122 -- the owner's default: notice, sale and foreclosure`

@export The owner is in default: may I serve a notice to pay (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage is registered
      `months the owner's default has continued` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months the owner's default has continued
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage expressly fixes before a notice to pay, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I serve a notice to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my lender serve a notice to pay` `the mortgage is registered` `months the owner's default has continued` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The owner is in default: is my notice to pay properly served (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 106(2): personally, by registered post, left on the land, or a prescribed electronic way; ordinary post is not service)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `how the notice was sent` IS A Service @desc How the lender sent or gave the notice to pay
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my notice to pay properly served` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was the notice properly served on me` `how the notice was sent`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The owner is in default: may I sell the land (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 106-108)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the money is payable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage makes the money payable on demand
      `a written demand was made under the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender made a written demand under the mortgage
      `a notice to pay was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender served a notice to pay
      `how the notice was sent` IS A Service @desc How the lender sent or gave the notice to pay
      `months the default continued after the notice or demand` IS A NUMBER @desc Months the default has continued since the notice or demand
      `months fixed by the mortgage for sale` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage fixes after notice before sale, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I sell the mortgaged land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my lender sell my land` `the money is payable on demand` `a written demand was made under the mortgage` `a notice to pay was served` `how the notice was sent` `months the default continued after the notice or demand` `months fixed by the mortgage for sale`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export I have sold the land under my power of sale: how much of the sale money must I pay the owner as the surplus (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 109(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the sale price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price the land sold for, in dollars
      `the expenses of the sale and default` IS A NUMBER @desc The expenses of and incidental to the sale and consequent on the default, in dollars
      `what is owing on the mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is due or owing on the mortgage under which the land was sold, in dollars
      `what is owing on later mortgages and charges` IS A NUMBER @desc What is owing on mortgages and charges registered after it, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the sale money must I pay the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN amount (`How much of the sale money comes to me` `the sale price` `the expenses of the sale and default` `what is owing on the mortgage` `what is owing on later mortgages and charges`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The owner is in default: may I apply to the Commissioner to foreclose the owner's right to redeem (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 121: 6 months' default and a failed auction first)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `months the default has continued after the time for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the time for payment in the mortgage, with the default continuing
      `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensed auctioneer offered the land at public auction after a notice to pay was served under s 106
      `the auction raised too little or drew no bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the highest bid was not enough to pay the mortgage money and expenses, or there was no bid
      `notice of intention to foreclose was served on the mortgagor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgagor (the owner) was served with notice of the lender's intention to apply for foreclosure
      `notice was served on every later registered interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone with a later interest on the Register was served with the same notice
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I apply to foreclose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my lender apply to foreclose` `months the default has continued after the time for payment` `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay` `the auction raised too little or drew no bid` `notice of intention to foreclose was served on the mortgagor` `notice was served on every later registered interest`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export The owner is in default: may a foreclosure order now issue to me, vesting the land in me free of the right to redeem (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 122)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner is in default under my mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has failed to pay money due under your mortgage, or to keep one of its covenants, and the failure continues
      `the Commissioner directed the advertisements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed the advertisements offering the land for private sale
      `months since the first advertisement` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the first advertisement
      `the time the Commissioner appointed has come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time the Commissioner appointed (at least one month after the first advertisement) has arrived
      `a sale in the interval raised enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sale in the meantime raised enough to pay the principal, interest and all expenses
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May a foreclosure order issue to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I lent money on a mortgage of someone's land` THEN
        IF `the owner is in default under my mortgage`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can a foreclosure order issue against me` `the Commissioner directed the advertisements` `months since the first advertisement` `the time the Commissioner appointed has come` `a sale in the interval raised enough`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the caveator`

§§§ `ss 138-142 -- my caveat`

-- s 139 meets every caveator whose caveat is met by a dealing, so this question takes no situation input.
@export Does my caveat stop the owner's dealing being registered (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 139, 142)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat forbidding the dealing is in force on the title
      `it was lodged after the instrument was presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your caveat was lodged after the instrument was presented for registration
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises the dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a beneficiary's caveat: whether the Commissioner is of opinion the will or settlement authorises the dealing
      `I consent to the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you consent to the registration of the dealing
      `days since I was served with notice of the dealing` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you were served with notice of the dealing
      `I protested in writing within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a written protest within 14 days of being served
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my caveat block the dealing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` THEN `yes if` (`Does the caveat stop my dealing` `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing` `it was lodged after the instrument was presented` `the kind of caveat` `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises the dealing` `I consent to the registration` `days since I was served with notice of the dealing` `I protested in writing within 14 days`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 138(3): the 14 days run from the notice served on the caveator, so that notice is the situation. The application
-- standing is the baseline's own input, asked as "has not been withdrawn".
@export The owner has applied to register a dealing: has my caveat lapsed, 14 days after I was served with notice of it (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 138(3), (4); a beneficiary's caveat and the Registrar's do not lapse this way)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have been served with notice that the owner has applied to register a dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been served with notice that the registered proprietor has applied to register a transfer or other dealing affecting the caveated land
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the owner's application has not been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner's application to register the dealing still stands (it has not been withdrawn)
      `days since the caveator was served with notice of the application` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the caveator was served with notice of the application to register the dealing
      `a judge has ordered a further delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge, on the caveator's undertaking or security, directed the Registrar to delay registration
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my caveat lapsed on the owner's application` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` THEN
        IF `I have been served with notice that the owner has applied to register a dealing`
        THEN `yes if` (`Has the caveat lapsed on my dealing` `the kind of caveat` `the owner's application has not been withdrawn` `days since the caveator was served with notice of the application` `a judge has ordered a further delay`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 138B: the notice served on the caveator is the situation, so the baseline's `the Registrar served the caveator with
-- my notice` is TRUE by the situation's own terms.
@export I have been served with a notice that my caveat will lapse in 21 days: has it lapsed (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 138A, 138B: unless I obtain a Supreme Court order extending it and lodge a copy)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the Registrar has served me with a notice that my caveat will lapse in 21 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar, on the owner's application, has served you with a notice under s 138B that your caveat will lapse unless you act within 21 days
      `the kind of caveat` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `days since the 21-day notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the s 138B notice was served on the caveator
      `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator obtained a Supreme Court order extending the caveat and lodged a copy with the Registrar
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Has my caveat lapsed on the 21-day notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` THEN
        IF `the Registrar has served me with a notice that my caveat will lapse in 21 days`
        THEN `yes if` (`Has the caveat lapsed on my notice` `the kind of caveat` TRUE `days since the 21-day notice was served` `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export My caveat has ended: may I lodge another caveat over the same land (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 138D: not after a 21-day notice, without the owner's endorsed consent or the Supreme Court's leave)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `my earlier caveat over this land has come to an end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat you lodged over this land has been withdrawn, has lapsed, or has been ended by the Supreme Court
      `how the caveat ended` IS A CaveatEnd @desc How the earlier caveat came to an end
      `the owner's consent is endorsed on the new caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the registered proprietor's consent is endorsed on the further caveat
      `the Supreme Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court gave leave for the further caveat and the order was served on the Registrar
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I caveat the land again` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` THEN
        IF `my earlier caveat over this land has come to an end`
        THEN `yes if` (`May the caveator lodge another caveat` `how the caveat ended` `the owner's consent is endorsed on the new caveat` `the Supreme Court gave leave`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I be made to compensate someone for lodging my caveat without reasonable cause (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) s 140; the amount is for a judge)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Seat @desc Which of these describes you
      `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause
      `someone suffered damage from my caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner, or anyone else, suffered damage because of your caveat, for example a lost or delayed sale
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be made to pay compensation for my caveat` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I claim an interest in someone's land and have lodged a caveat` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be compensated for the caveat` `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` `someone suffered damage from my caveat`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
